WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.100
We’re in Manila now.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.380
This is our first night here.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.060
Before... Nom!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.300
I forgot what I was going to say.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.860
Before tomorrow’s show.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.700
We went out to eat.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.760
What did we eat? Stir-fried morning glory?

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.600
Was that morning glory?

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:49.860
I liked that one.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.280
It was grilled squid, 
like the grilled pork skewers we have back home.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.460
It was just like grilled pork skewers, 
but it was grilled squid.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.840
That’s enough. My throat hurts.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.840
(I do want to eat it, though.)

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.180
See? The end.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.180
And there was stir-fried pork with black olive paste.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.520
Someone said they wanted rice porridge.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.380
Seriously, I really want rice porridge.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.280
It’s my first time.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.520
It’s the first time. 
By the time we got here, it was already dark.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.120
Yeah.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.260
The sunlight was so beautiful while Bonnie was asleep.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.160
(Was the sun the pretty thing?)

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:17.920
The light was so pretty.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.180
What do you mean 
I was asleep while the sunlight was beautiful?

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.480
The fans are so cute.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.200
Yes.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.380
Their energy already looked so ready.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.020
Ready to listen to us.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.500
I really want to hear 
how loudly the fans are going to sing tomorrow.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.040
Because both of us have really sore throats.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.440
My throat hurts. Help.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.340
I’m expecting everyone to be super energetic.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.200
(Are you two fully boosted up yet?)

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:43.800
No.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.220
(You’re already fully boosted.)

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.220
Bonnie has to stop feeding me snacks first.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.840
Here it comes.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.280
P’Emi doesn’t like eating rice. 
She’ll only eat the snacks I feed her.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.800
Didn’t you say that was the last piece?

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.560
Then did you eat just now?

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.080
I did.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.120
The one P’Nok brought for me.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.860
That’s enough. My throat hurts.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.680
See?

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.440
No way. As soon as P’Nok feeds you, you eat it.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.040
You have to feed her.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.300
Emi, what color do you want? 
What color do you feel like eating?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.240
Stuff like that.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.100
My throat hurts.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.640
It’s really starting to hurt now.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.840
My name is Emi, like this?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.580
Emi?

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.000
I have...

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:36.800
Are you making up a song?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.660
Kitty?

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.580
What do you call pajamas again?

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.460
There you go.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.700
You’re good.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.260
I love Emi-Bonnie~

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.140
Yeah.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.600
What about my song?

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.400
My name is Bonnie.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.720
What’s good about Bonnie, Emi?

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.480
Long hair.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.260
That vowel sound again.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.800
I have wink-wink eyes.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.060
My kid is a butterfly.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.140
Emi-Bonnie never die!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.300
You’re good.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.100
I love Emi and ANY.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.600
See you tomorrow!

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.720
See you!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.140
♪ Please listen close ‘cause this is my truth ♪

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.540
♪ I just love you this way ♪

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.840
Emi! Emi!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.940
♪ My name is Emi ♪

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.460
No!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.420
♪ I just love Emi ♪

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.760
Emi! Emi!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.860
That actually works.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.000
Emi! Sing that part!

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.400
Let’s guess the profession.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:44.780
This card is for you

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:45.780
A frog prince.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:47.880
A frog prince.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:48.820
(Again?)

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.780
Because the shirt is green.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:51.740
Future profession?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:55.880
The dream future profession is to become a prince.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.360
There’s even a wand. Look.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.320
It’s a magic wand too, for turning frogs into people.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.580
Is this game over already?

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.020
It is.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.200
Next, P’Toon.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.380
(There’s only one card I picked.)

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:05.760
This?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.240
Yes.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.400
A spy.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.220
A spy because of the headscarf.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.220
Wearing a headscarf, 
holding documents, and making this face.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.960
Here, let me show you.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:22.780
A keeper of secrets.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.520
Let me see.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.280
And he’s making this sly face.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.300
This document is the secret being kept.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.560
And the headscarf is for disguise.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.600
It’s a GMMTV document.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.000
(Hey, this one.)

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.240
Another prince.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.220
A rival prince from the opposing kingdom.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.580
The last one was a frog prince. This one is, well...

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.580
A duck prince.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.720
P’Nok is a royal guard.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.640
This guard is serving both princes.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.160
A two-headed bird.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.340
Hello!

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:02.980
Where are you going?

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.540
Going to talk first. Hello?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.160
(It’s over.)

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.480
The prince has gone off to work.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.100
And lastly, I picked this one for myself.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.540
Also a royal guard.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.700
Standing on the side and knowing the whole truth.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.580
(Another two-headed bird, too?)

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.220
Yes, exactly the same.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.860
(Are you going to report it to the king?)

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:20.620
The king? Oh, right.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.280
(What’s his name again?)

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:22.980
His name is Ueng.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.040
And then choosing the side of the next king, 
and in the end becoming nothing at all.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.440
This is the one who will get the throne.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.320
The real one.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.260
Have you ever watched Battle of Fates or something?

